{
  "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
  "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Victor S. Haltom",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HALTOM: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The constitutional error that occurred in Mr. Fry's third trial is the type of error that can result in a conviction of an innocent person."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I suppose he could have come here on direct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But for the former, you are perfectly content with our applying Kotteakos. And for the latter, however, you say we have to apply Chapman."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You're now arguing that under Brecht this should not have been harmless; is that the point you're making?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You think it means, does it matter in this case which harmless -- you think that second sentence means would, would the defendant be entitled to reversal of the conviction no matter which harmless error standard is employed? You think that's what it means?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: To talk about burdens of proof?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Haltom",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HALTOM: I think that that's a question, Your Honor, that this court has struggled with. As Justice Scalia pointed out in his concurring opinion in Dominguez Benitez, that we're talking about with these harmless error standards ineffable gradations of probability that are beyond even the judicial mind to grasp."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Are you talking about what's on the bottom of page 181 of the joint appendix? That was the only place that I found where the magistrate expressed a view on this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Suppose we apply Brecht."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How did Hurtz's name enter into the trial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if Maples' testimony had come in, I presume they could have cross-examined him on the basis of Maples' testimony?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask two questions and then you can proceed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Millett",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5247",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "69c6a05c7d20dc67b63dd1aef03c1c164c5a98f935ff6541d1a9e3f0034321da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-69c6a05c7d20-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that in no sense does this record support the notion, support the argument, that there was a substantial and injurious effect when the twelfth out of eleven witnesses was excluded, talking about third party culpability."
    },
    {
